WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.456
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.756 --> 00:00:07.725
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.025 --> 00:00:13.974
Unit thirty-one: Style and Identity. In this unit, you will talk about fashion, appearance and services.

4
00:00:14.983 --> 00:00:16.124
fashion trend.

5
00:00:16.824 --> 00:00:20.565
fashion trend means a style that is popular at a particular time.

6
00:00:20.865 --> 00:00:23.607
Oversized shirts are a big fashion trend this year.

7
00:00:24.307 --> 00:00:26.402
Your turn. Say: fashion trend.

8
00:00:29.102 --> 00:00:30.312
fashion trend.

9
00:00:31.317 --> 00:00:32.260
outfit.

10
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.273
outfit means a set of clothes worn together.

11
00:00:35.573 --> 00:00:37.677
She wore a beautiful outfit to the wedding.

12
00:00:38.377 --> 00:00:40.681
Your turn. Say: outfit.

13
00:00:43.381 --> 00:00:44.185
outfit.

14
00:00:45.183 --> 00:00:45.975
hairstyle.

15
00:00:46.675 --> 00:00:49.128
hairstyle means the way your hair is cut and arranged.

16
00:00:49.428 --> 00:00:51.822
He changed his hairstyle for his new job.

17
00:00:52.522 --> 00:00:55.070
Your turn. Say: hairstyle.

18
00:00:57.770 --> 00:00:58.841
hairstyle.

19
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:00.805
dress code.

20
00:01:01.505 --> 00:01:04.410
dress code means rules about what clothes you must wear.

21
00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:06.709
The office has a smart dress code.

22
00:01:07.409 --> 00:01:09.504
Your turn. Say: dress code.

23
00:01:12.204 --> 00:01:13.322
dress code.

24
00:01:14.317 --> 00:01:15.527
second-hand clothes.

25
00:01:16.227 --> 00:01:20.374
second-hand clothes means clothes that someone else owned before.

26
00:01:20.674 --> 00:01:23.301
Second-hand clothes are cheaper and better for the planet.

27
00:01:24.001 --> 00:01:26.688
Your turn. Say: second-hand clothes.

28
00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:30.935
second-hand clothes.

29
00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:32.626
brand.

30
00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:35.627
brand means the name of a company's products.

31
00:01:35.927 --> 00:01:38.182
Which brand of sneakers do you prefer?

32
00:01:38.882 --> 00:01:40.768
Your turn. Say: brand.

33
00:01:43.468 --> 00:01:44.191
brand.

34
00:01:45.183 --> 00:01:46.324
accessories.

35
00:01:47.024 --> 00:01:50.881
accessories means extra items like bags, belts and jewellery.

36
00:01:51.181 --> 00:01:53.923
She always matches her accessories with her shoes.

37
00:01:54.623 --> 00:01:57.009
Your turn. Say: accessories.

38
00:01:59.709 --> 00:02:01.070
accessories.

39
00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:02.899
makeover.

40
00:02:03.599 --> 00:02:06.666
makeover means a big change in someone's appearance.

41
00:02:06.966 --> 00:02:09.825
Before the graduation, Nita had a complete makeover.

42
00:02:10.525 --> 00:02:12.527
Your turn. Say: makeover.

43
00:02:15.227 --> 00:02:16.298
makeover.

44
00:02:17.283 --> 00:02:19.178
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:19.478 --> 00:02:20.712
You look different, Nita!

46
00:02:22.017 --> 00:02:26.343
Thanks! I had my hair cut yesterday. It's a new hairstyle.

47
00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:30.093
It suits you. Is that a new outfit too?

48
00:02:31.383 --> 00:02:35.394
Yes, but it's second-hand. I'm getting the trousers shortened next week.

49
00:02:36.683 --> 00:02:39.905
Smart choice. Is there a dress code at your internship?

50
00:02:41.217 --> 00:02:45.448
Yes, smart casual. I'm having my shoes repaired so I can wear them there.

51
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.585
Grammar focus: have / get something done.

52
00:02:49.885 --> 00:02:54.996
Use have or get, plus object, plus past participle when someone does a service for you.

53
00:02:55.296 --> 00:02:58.086
For example: I had my hair cut yesterday.

54
00:02:58.386 --> 00:03:00.292
Get is a little more informal than have.

55
00:03:00.592 --> 00:03:04.217
Use this structure when you pay or ask someone else to do a job for you.

56
00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:08.322
Now read and listen. The Rise of Second-Hand Fashion.

57
00:03:08.622 --> 00:03:12.432
Fashion trends change faster than ever, but this creates a lot of waste.

58
00:03:13.717 --> 00:03:17.702
Many young Cambodians are now buying second-hand clothes at markets and online.

59
00:03:19.017 --> 00:03:22.595
Instead of buying new, some people get old clothes repaired or redesigned.

60
00:03:23.883 --> 00:03:28.437
A small change, like new accessories, can give an outfit a complete makeover.

61
00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:33.874
Experts say that personal style matters more than any famous brand.

62
00:03:35.183 --> 00:03:37.812
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:38.112 --> 00:03:40.634
Rules about what clothes you must wear are a blank.

64
00:03:40.934 --> 00:03:44.472
A, dress code. B, brand. C, fashion trend.

65
00:03:48.483 --> 00:03:50.436
The answer is A: dress code.

66
00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:54.275
I blank my phone screen repaired last week.

67
00:03:54.575 --> 00:03:57.346
A, had. B, have done. C, did.

68
00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:02.746
The answer is A: had.

69
00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.110
She is getting her hair blank tomorrow.

70
00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:09.286
A, cut. B, cutting. C, to cut.

71
00:04:13.283 --> 00:04:14.888
The answer is A: cut.

72
00:04:16.383 --> 00:04:18.975
Extra items like bags and belts are blank.

73
00:04:19.275 --> 00:04:22.975
A, outfits. B, accessories. C, makeovers.

74
00:04:26.983 --> 00:04:29.087
The answer is B: accessories.

75
00:04:30.583 --> 00:04:34.057
According to the text, what matters more than a famous brand?

76
00:04:34.357 --> 00:04:37.709
A, price. B, personal style. C, colour.

77
00:04:41.717 --> 00:04:44.053
The answer is B: personal style.

78
00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:49.201
Now it's your turn to speak. What services do you pay for regularly?

79
00:04:54.501 --> 00:04:58.753
I have my hair cut every month, and I get my motorbike checked twice a year.

80
00:04:59.053 --> 00:05:00.507
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:01.517 --> 00:05:05.400
Great work today! You learned eight new words and have / get something done.

82
00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.967
Today's value is self-confidence. Believe in yourself.

83
00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:11.699
See you in Unit thirty-two. Goodbye!

84
00:05:11.999 --> 00:05:15.290
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

